        "original_id": "7c87d548-7fdc-548b-b8b2-611b0a03ec8e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Heaney, Franklin D. Roosevelt\n- Organizations: Works Progress Administration\n- Places: Timberline Lodge, Mount Hood, Clackamas County, Government Camp, Estacada, Oregon\n- Systems: Oregon Route 173, U.S. Route 26, Beaver Oaks Airport\n\nFacts:\n- During the Great Depression in the 1930s, Charles Heaney worked as an artist for the Works Progress Administration.\n- During the 1930s, Charles Heaney created several works featuring Mount Hood and Timberline Lodge.\n- Timberline Lodge was dedicated on September 28, 1937, by President Franklin D. Roosevelt.\n- Oregon Route 173 is an Oregon state highway that runs from Timberline Lodge in Clackamas County to U.S. Route 26 near Government Camp.\n- Beaver Oaks Airport, with FAA LID OR66, is a private airport located 3 miles northwest of Estacada in Clackamas County, Oregon, USA.",
